goeval -h

-- exit status: 1 --
-- stderr --

Usage: goeval [<options>...] <code> [<args>...]

Options:
  -E	just dump the assembled source, without running it.
  -Eplay
    	just dump the assembled source for posting on https://go.dev/play
  -go string
    	go command path. (default "go")
  -goimports string
    	goimports tool name, to use an alternate tool or just disable it. (default "goimports")
  -i value
    	* import package local package from GOPATH:  [alias=]import-path
    	* import package in Go module mode:          [alias=]import-path@version
    	Once a version is mentioned, Go module mode is enabled globally.
  -o value
    	just build a binary, don't execute.
  -play
    	run the code remotely on https://go.dev/play
  -share
    	share the code on https://go.dev/play and print the URL.
  -x	print commands executed.

Example:
  goeval -i fmt 'fmt.Println("Hello, world!")'

